.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-KEYS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-keys
.Nd the key store: other people's keys by name
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis keys
.Op Fl -store Ar dir
.Cm list
.Op Ar name
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm find
.Ar name
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm add
.Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl e Ar email
.Ar key.pub
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm add
.Fl -card Ar file
.Ar key.pub
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm certify
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar cert
.Op Fl -force
.Ar name
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm addcert
.Ar cert
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm trust
.Ar name
.Ar level
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm export
.Op Fl o Ar key.pub
.Op Fl -force
.Ar name
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm bundle
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl -force
.Ar name
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm import
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm fetch
.Op Fl -url
.Ar email
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm rm
.Ar name
.Nm noqtis keys
.Cm path
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The key store is a folder of other people's public keys, signature keys
and KEM keys alike, each under the name and e-mail address of its
holder.
It also holds certifications, by which the holder of one key says that
another key belongs to its name, and the trust its owner places in each
holder to make such statements.
From these it works out which keys are
.Em valid :
known to belong to their names.
.Pp
Where a command takes a public key file, with
.Fl p
or
.Fl s ,
.Ql @ Ns Ar name
takes a valid key of the store instead:
.Dl noqtis box -p @ben -o notes.nqk notes.txt
.Pp
A
.Ar name
is part of a name or of an address, letters of either case alike, or
the start of a fingerprint, 8 hex digits or more.
.Cm list
shows every key that answers it; the other commands, and
.Ql @ Ns Ar name ,
need exactly one key to answer.
.Pp
The commands:
.Bl -tag -width "certify"
.It Cm list Op Ar name
Print one line for each key: the first 16 digits of its fingerprint
(the SHA-256 of the public key), its algorithm, its trust, its
validity, the number of certifications of it, and its name and
address;
.Ql [card]
when the store holds its identity card.
.It Cm find Ar name
As
.Cm list ,
with exit status 1 when no key answers.
.It Cm add
Put the key in
.Ar key.pub
into the store, under
.Fl n Ar name
and, when given,
.Fl e Ar email ,
or with the identity card
.Pq Xr noqtis-idcard 1
in
.Fl -card Ar file ,
which must verify and name this key; the name and address are then the
card's.
A key that is there already keeps its trust and takes the new name;
certifications of the old name no longer count.
.It Cm certify
Sign, with the secret signature key
.Ar key
(and
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub
beside it), that the one key answering
.Ar name
belongs to the name and address the store has for it.
Do this once the fingerprint was compared with its holder over a
channel that cannot be forged.
The certification is kept in the store and, with
.Fl o ,
written to
.Ar cert
to give to others.
.Fl -pass-fd
and
.Fl -pass-env
give the passphrase of a protected
.Ar key .
.It Cm addcert Ar cert
Put a certification someone else made into the store.
The key it certifies and the key that made it must both be there, the
first under the name and address it says, and its signature must
verify.
.It Cm trust Ar name Ar level
Say how far the holder of the key is trusted to certify other keys:
.Cm unknown ,
.Cm never ,
.Cm marginal ,
.Cm full ,
or
.Cm ultimate
for your own keys.
.It Cm export Ar name
Write the key as a key file to
.Fl o Ar key.pub ,
or to standard output.
.It Cm bundle Ar name
Write a key bundle to
.Fl o Ar file ,
or to standard output: the identity card of the one signature key
answering
.Ar name ,
then every other key that key certified under its own name and address
(a KEM key to seal to its holder, a second signature key), each with
the certification, as armored text
.Pq Xr noqtis-armor 1 .
The key must have its card in the store.
This is what to publish, or to send.
.It Cm import Ar file
Put the keys of a bundle into the store.
The card must verify, and every key after it must come with a
certification by the card's key that verifies and says the card's name
and address.
Nothing a bundle brings is valid for that alone: certify the card's key
once its fingerprint was compared with its holder.
.It Cm fetch Ar email
Look the address up at its own domain and import the bundle found
there, over https:
.Dl https://<domain>/.well-known/noqtis/<hash>
where the hash is the first 20 bytes, in hex, of the SHA-256 of the
part before the
.Ql @
in lower case.
The card must be for
.Ar email .
A domain publishes a holder's keys by serving the output of
.Cm bundle
there.
With
.Fl -url
the address is printed and nothing is fetched.
.It Cm rm Ar name
Remove the key, its card, and every certification of it and by it.
.It Cm path
Print the folder of the store.
.El
.Pp
A key is valid when its trust is
.Cm ultimate ;
or when it was certified by one valid key whose trust is
.Cm full
or
.Cm ultimate ,
or by three valid keys of trust
.Cm marginal .
One or two marginal certifications make it marginally valid, which is
not enough for
.Ql @ Ns Ar name .
Certifications are followed five keys deep from an ultimately trusted
one, only signature keys certify, and a key's certification of itself
does not count.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -store Ar dir
The folder of the store.
Default: the value of
.Ev NOQTIS_KEYS ,
else
.Pa noqtis/keys
under
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
or
.Pa ~/.config
.Po
.Ev APPDATA
on Windows
.Pc .
.Cm add
makes the folder when it is not there.
.El
.Pp
The store is its owner's own state and is not signed: whoever can write
the folder decides what it trusts.
A card's and a certification's signature, and a key's fingerprint, are
checked when they are put in.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width NOQTIS_KEYS
.It Ev NOQTIS_KEYS
The folder of the key store.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when
.Cm find
finds no key, or what
.Cm addcert ,
.Cm import
or
.Cm fetch
was given does not verify; 2 on a usage, file or network error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
$ noqtis keys add -n "Ben Example" -e ben@example.org ben.pub
$ noqtis keys trust me ultimate
$ noqtis keys certify -k me ben
$ noqtis box -p @ben -o notes.nqk notes.txt
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-box 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-idcard 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-verify 1 ,
